WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.990
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:08.642
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:15.286
Unit twenty-two: Healthy Lifestyle Choices. Today you will use gerunds as subjects to talk about health.

4
00:00:15.586 --> 00:00:18.018
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:22.118
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:24.124
Lifestyle.

7
00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:27.023
Lifestyle means the way you live.

8
00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:29.848
My grandfather has an active lifestyle.

9
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.137
Your turn. Say: Lifestyle.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.245
Lifestyle.

11
00:00:37.983 --> 00:00:38.996
Choice.

12
00:00:39.983 --> 00:00:42.482
Choice means a decision between options.

13
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:44.793
Water is a healthy choice.

14
00:00:45.383 --> 00:00:47.757
Your turn. Say: Choice.

15
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.508
Choice.

16
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.414
Exercise.

17
00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:57.508
Exercise means physical activity to stay healthy.

18
00:00:58.117 --> 00:01:00.174
Exercise makes me feel happy.

19
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:03.587
Your turn. Say: Exercise.

20
00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.655
Exercise.

21
00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:09.186
Diet.

22
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:12.253
Diet means the food you usually eat.

23
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:15.802
My diet includes lots of fish and vegetables.

24
00:01:16.417 --> 00:01:18.756
Your turn. Say: Diet.

25
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.450
Diet.

26
00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:24.102
Sleep.

27
00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:28.033
Sleep means rest when your eyes are closed at night.

28
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:31.009
Teenagers need eight to ten hours of sleep.

29
00:01:31.617 --> 00:01:34.524
Your turn. Say: Sleep.

30
00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:38.217
Sleep.

31
00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:39.973
Stress.

32
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:43.645
Stress means a feeling of worry and pressure.

33
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.168
Exams cause stress.

34
00:01:46.783 --> 00:01:49.111
Your turn. Say: Stress.

35
00:01:51.967 --> 00:01:53.455
Stress.

36
00:01:54.217 --> 00:01:55.090
Habit.

37
00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:58.536
Habit means something you do regularly.

38
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:00.999
Drinking water is a good habit.

39
00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:03.922
Your turn. Say: Habit.

40
00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:07.559
Habit.

41
00:02:08.317 --> 00:02:09.469
Balance.

42
00:02:10.483 --> 00:02:13.203
Balance means a healthy mix of different things.

43
00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:15.723
Balance is the key to health.

44
00:02:16.317 --> 00:02:18.690
Your turn. Say: Balance.

45
00:02:21.533 --> 00:02:22.627
Balance.

46
00:02:23.433 --> 00:02:27.340
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.183 --> 00:02:30.787
Visal, what healthy choice could you make this week?

48
00:02:31.883 --> 00:02:36.823
I could exercise more. Exercising regularly reduces stress.

49
00:02:37.917 --> 00:02:40.023
Good. What about your diet?

50
00:02:41.117 --> 00:02:43.790
Eating more vegetables is my next goal.

51
00:02:44.883 --> 00:02:45.838
And sleep?

52
00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:51.155
Going to bed earlier is hard, but it's a good habit!

53
00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:53.835
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:54.683 --> 00:02:57.205
Grammar focus: Gerunds as subjects.

55
00:02:57.505 --> 00:02:58.588
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:59.283 --> 00:03:01.829
Exercising regularly reduces stress.

57
00:03:02.717 --> 00:03:04.844
Eating vegetables is good for you.

58
00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.773
Sleeping well helps your memory.

59
00:03:08.733 --> 00:03:12.707
A gerund subject is singular: Exercising reduces stress.

60
00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:17.902
Be careful! Don't say: Exercise regularly reduces stress.

61
00:03:19.867 --> 00:03:23.062
Say: Exercising regularly reduces stress.

62
00:03:23.362 --> 00:03:25.884
Use the -ing form when a verb is the subject.

63
00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.236
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:32.161
Small Choices, Big Results.

65
00:03:32.461 --> 00:03:35.412
A healthy lifestyle depends on every choice we make.

66
00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.189
Exercising regularly reduces stress.

67
00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.780
Eating a balanced diet gives us energy.

68
00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:46.335
Getting enough sleep helps our body and mind.

69
00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:50.401
Building good habits helps us keep a healthy balance.

70
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.409
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.563
blank regularly reduces stress.

72
00:03:58.863 --> 00:04:03.387
A, Exercising. B, Exercise to. C, Exercises.

73
00:04:06.933 --> 00:04:09.560
The answer is A: Exercising.

74
00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.832
The food you usually eat is your blank.

75
00:04:13.132 --> 00:04:16.728
A, diet. B, lifestyle. C, habit.

76
00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.034
The answer is A: diet.

77
00:04:23.183 --> 00:04:25.659
A decision between options is a blank.

78
00:04:25.959 --> 00:04:29.229
A, choice. B, balance. C, stress.

79
00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:34.801
The answer is A: choice.

80
00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.198
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.317
Which healthy choice could you make this week?

82
00:04:51.117 --> 00:04:52.443
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:52.743 --> 00:05:00.132
I could drink more water this week. Drinking water instead of soft drinks is a healthy choice, and it saves money too.

84
00:05:00.432 --> 00:05:02.095
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:07.261
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and gerunds as subjects.

86
00:05:07.561 --> 00:05:12.001
Today's value is self-care. Look after yourself and rest when you are sick.

87
00:05:12.301 --> 00:05:15.790
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

88
00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:18.846
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

